{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>He divided against them by night.</b> That is to say, it grew dark, and even so he did not refrain from pursuing them until midnight." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Abraham: You slew My enemies from midnight until morning; by your life, I shall slay the enemies of your children from midnight until morning, as is said (Exodus 11): ״כחצות הלילה אני יוצא בתוך מצרים״. This Midrash indicates that his battle was from midnight until morning." "<b>And according to</b> the plain sense of the verse, it appears to me that all night long his heart did not rest nor did he see sleep; rather, he was occupied fighting against them all night — half the night he pursued and half he smote. And this is the sense of <b>he divided against them by night, he and his servants, and smote them and pursued them</b> — that is to say, he smote them in the latter half after he had pursued them in the first half." "<b>Until Hobah.</b> Until they acknowledged their guilt — for a punishment befell them from the left side, and it became clear to them that they were held liable in the realm of strict justice; in the manner of what is written (Genesis 44): ״האלהים מצא את עון עבדיך״. And therefore they fell by the left side of Eliezer, who was striking them; this is the sense of משמאל לדמשק — 'on the left of Damascus' — for the word משמאל governs both what precedes and what follows, and it is thus to be interpreted: 'until חובה, which is on the left,' and likewise 'on the left of Damascus.' And you will find a parallel (Psalms 50): ״מציון מכלל יופי״ — a phrase that serves both what is above and what is below."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:24.020529040Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}